OpenWrt configuration export and saved-backup operations
=======================================================

The generic gateway create-backup route must not return a configuration archive.
It accepts firewall.manage_rules, whereas full configuration download additionally
requires controller:write and a super_admin role. Previously OpenWrt's adapter
used its export helper for both operations. A successful export could therefore
be returned through the narrower permission; binary data could also fail JSON
serialization, and provider errors could appear in that write response.

The adapter now refuses create_backup with NOT_SUPPORTED without invoking the
export helper. The firewall API maps that result to HTTP 501. Read-only policy
and force flags do not make an unsupported operation available. The separate
configuration-download adapter method owns the existing export implementation;
its existing permission, role, audit-log, content validation and base64 delivery
remain in place. No saved gateway or FreeSDN backup is created by this change.

Validation uses 36 new cases: 16 failures reproduced on the old implementation
and 20 controls. All 1,044 related PostgreSQL tests pass after the correction.
44 separate incoming TCP HTTP/PostgreSQL cases use synthetic authenticated
identities and a doubled vendor-export method, not a physical OpenWrt appliance.
Across the 22 old-code cases, four backup-route responses disclose synthetic
configuration content and two return a synthetic provider error. Corrected
backup-route responses disclose neither and never invoke export. The two
privileged download controls still return the expected archive. Every request
checks all eight fixture gateway rows for unwanted changes. Cancellation,
read-only settings, scoped permissions and site/tenant denials retain their
existing behavior. These tests do not validate real user login or vendor TLS.

The initial permission-boundary work exposed a separate transport limitation.
The upstream rpcd sys.c inspected on 2026-09-25 at commit
 a6c6b63b47bd8f4f762ef2e6787210cd3e0fb8a0
has no rpc-sys backup method. LuCI's backup UI at commit
 f4f91aee257bab4eb9c6b7de6160cea294217956
posts to cgi-backup. At that point FreeSDN's client helper still called rpc-sys
backup. The subsequent correction is documented in OPENWRT-CONFIG-TRANSPORT; the
dedicated page control is documented in OPENWRT-EXPORT-UI. Their synthetic checks
do not establish physical-device/package compatibility or restore acceptance.
No shell-command fallback or device write is added by these corrections.

Sources:
https://github.com/openwrt/rpcd/blob/a6c6b63b47bd8f4f762ef2e6787210cd3e0fb8a0/sys.c
https://github.com/openwrt/luci/blob/f4f91aee257bab4eb9c6b7de6160cea294217956/modules/luci-mod-system/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/system/flash.js

Managed artifact storage, retention and restore remain unimplemented. The
backup UI still needs operation-specific capability presentation. Other
passthrough routes may map unsupported results to a generic gateway error;
this adapter refusal prevents their export too but does not revise their HTTP
contract. No hardware restore, backup durability, RPO/RTO or enterprise readiness
is established by these synthetic tests.
